' Final OO principles mapping note (references used above)
note bottom
  Encapsulation: Private fields ("-") + public accessors ("+") in model classes.
  Inheritance (is-a): Shown with --|> arrows (User -> Student/CompanyRepresentative/Staff).
  Composition: Repositories *-- domain objects (explicit multiplicity "1" to "0..*").
  Aggregation: CompanyRepresentative o-- InternshipOpportunity indicates shared ownership.
  Dependency Inversion: Services depend on repository abstractions (LoginService -> UserRepository).
  Business Logic: InternshipService filters by year (Year 1-2: BASIC; Year 3-4: All) and major (case-insensitive).
  Withdrawal Enhancement: Students can withdraw from both PENDING and SUCCESSFUL applications.
  Self-Registration: Company representatives can register via LoginHandler (requires staff approval).
  Filter System: OpportunityFilterService applies user-configured filters (Status, Major, Level, Date).
  Filter Persistence: FilterStateManager maintains filter settings per user across menu navigation.
  Default Behavior: All opportunities sorted alphabetically by title.
end note

